{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"cea4959d-bd05-41ba-8e24-98c0638e62d2","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated the silent failure, fixed the issues in the configuration and review script, and documented the causes and colleague note analysis in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-hUHbF3/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Missing `USER` in launchd environment (`com.vk.nightly-review.plist`)**:\n   - `launchd` runs jobs without the `USER` environment variable by default. Headless CLI tools such as `claude` require `USER` to locate their login credentials in the macOS keychain, resulting in `Not logged in · Please run /login` on each run.\n   - **Fix**: Added `\u003ckey\u003eUSER\u003c/key\u003e\u003cstring\u003evk\u003c/string\u003e` under `EnvironmentVariables` in [com.vk.nightly-review.plist](file:///tmp/h-hUHbF3/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L23-L29).\n\n2. **Assignment to read-only variable `status` in zsh (`nightly-review.zsh`)**:\n   - In zsh, `status` is a read-only alias to `$?`. Assigning `status=$?` caused the shell to exit immediately with `/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status` before reaching the notification logic. This silenced all failure reports.\n   - **Fix**: Changed `status=$?` to `rc=$?` and updated references in [nightly-review.zsh](file:///tmp/h-hUHbF3/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24). Also added `\u003c /dev/null` to the `claude -p` invocation to prevent waiting on stdin under launchd.\n","duration_seconds":59.032392,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":215479,"output_tokens":2076,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":15037,"total_tokens":217555}}}
